      "r156": "An article?",
      "r157": "What are you fixing tiles for? We’re supposed to be choosing a festival attraction.",
      "r275": "With the cheating exposed, the game is over. Nobuhara asks for one more hand. All three girls shake their heads.",
      "r276": "We put the tiles away. Only the blank proposal remains on the desk. No winner. No festival attraction.",
      "r277": "Maybe that computer can at least help us find a festival idea. Once the classroom is tidy, we head back to the library.",
      "r158": "This calls for collective intelligence. Let’s ask the internet.",
      "r159": "What about the collective intelligence that just spent an hour playing mahjong?",
      "r160": "There’s an imageboard bookmarked in this browser.",
      "r161": "Kotoha opens the browser. A cream-colored page fills with tiny thumbnails, numbered posts, and people named Anonymous.",
      "r162": "What year is it again?",
      "r163": "2026. Problem?",
      "r164": "Did we leave this browser behind in 2005?",
      "r165": "As we peer at the screen, our teacher pokes his head through the doorway.",
      "r166": "Is this teh internet old-timers’ club?",
      "r167": "What happened to you, sir? Please go home.",
      "r168": "…Just posting to say I was here.",
      "r169": "Use the attendance register.",
      "r170": "The teacher reluctantly retreats into the hall. We decide not to ask whose bookmark this is.",
      "r171": "“All your base are belong to us”… Wait, I know this one!",
      "r172": "We’re looking for festival ideas.",
      "r173": "“School festival ideas. Help.” Someone else is having the same problem.",
      "r174": "“You are the man now, dog.” See? Encouragement. This place is helpful.",
